# Files exempt from tools/check-no-site-data.sh.
#
# Currently EMPTY, and worth keeping that way. Everything in this repository
# is scanned, including the scanner's own test file, which assembles its
# fixtures from fragments that individually match nothing so it stays inside
# coverage rather than being excluded from it.
#
# Before adding an entry, try that technique first. An exempt file is
# unscannable by definition, so it is exactly where a real identifier survives
# review -- that has already happened once here, with a live address sitting
# in a file the scanner was configured to skip.
#
# If an entry is genuinely unavoidable: one glob per line, matched against the
# repo-relative path, with a comment saying why. Adding one is in the same
# category as pushing with --no-verify and deserves a second pair of eyes.
#
# This file is deliberately not self-exempt: the one file that can disable
# checking must not be the one file nobody checks.
